<p>Efforts to end the two-month Iran conflict remained at an impasse on Tuesday after President Trump objected to Tehran’s latest proposal, which would leave talks on Iran’s nuclear programme until after the fighting ends and shipping disputes are resolved. A U.S. official said Trump wants nuclear issues addressed from the outset. Trump said Tehran was seeking quick U.S. action on the Strait of Hormuz while dealing with internal leadership strain; the sources said it was unclear how Iran conveyed that message, and Tehran had no immediate response. An Iranian army spokesperson told state media the Islamic Republic did not consider the war over, and normal shipping through the Gulf remained heavily disrupted.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/qexnB_5bN3oQyjL45q_kFoKvspUzm-vOhUjb1Ff_sN9bl5eJfCp2q8uePPXVpSSSJNIRYCABLYALWn1mPAlyD4KqQOw3NCbl-oTO_ZMgfxbozVxAqyTybI9wipsldcy9y9lYl0YGLcWijodWNgZpmkk7I-4DVjoTEWMJG532wlSF8UJF7C8AChXQHNjh6-UxdP3XADrifEFW-cFYLsnPdv4DzgqG47nKZj6GzG4pb41Nl5tDckEBnaCD4I96zyvPsGHcjM7P' alt='President Trump insists nuclear issues be addressed first to end the war in Iran.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>U.S. pressure: The Wall Street Journal, cited by several sources, reported Trump instructed aides to prepare for an extended blockade of Iran’s ports.</li><li>Shipping route: The Strait of Hormuz is a chokepoint for global energy supplies and, in peacetime, carries about one-fifth of world oil and gas trade.</li></ul><blockquote>Iran has just informed us that they are in a &#x27;State of Collapse&#x27;. They want us to &#x27;Open the Hormuz Strait,&#x27; as soon as possible, as they try to figure out their leadership situation (Which I believe they will be able to do!). - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>U.S. Secretary of State Marco Rubio: Rubio said Iran’s proposal was “better than what we thought they were going to submit,” but added that any deal had to prevent Iran from “sprinting towards a nuclear weapon.